title: Energy and time · how a session is built
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph Q["Two questions, defaulted from last time"]
    direction LR
    E["Energy<br/>how much do I have to give?"] ~~~ T["Time<br/>how long do I have?"]
  end
  subgraph TIME["Time sets the slots"]
    direction LR
    T1["Short ≈ 20 min<br/>fewer exercises, fewer sets"] ~~~ T2["Normal ≈ 35 min<br/>the rotation item as written"] ~~~ T3["Long ≈ 50 min<br/>more sets, then a bonus slot"]
    T4["Slots are priced by the timing model<br/>seconds per set × sets, learned from your taps<br/>trim sets before exercises until it fits"]
  end
  subgraph ENERGY["Energy fills the slots by cost"]
    direction LR
    E1["Easy<br/>average cost ≤ 2, nothing above 3<br/>one rung down, stop 2 to 3 reps shy<br/>never judged by the ladder"] ~~~ E2["Normal<br/>average about 3, one exercise may be 4 or 5<br/>your rung, aim for the top"] ~~~ E3["Hard<br/>at least half the slots at 4 or 5<br/>your rung, nothing in reserve, +1 set on main lifts"]
  end
  subgraph COST["Cost: one number per exercise, 1 to 5, editable"]
    direction LR
    C5["5 heavy compound, spine loaded<br/>deadlift · back squat"] ~~~ C4["4 big compound<br/>bench · pull-up · overhead press"] ~~~ C3["3 bodyweight compound<br/>pike push-up · lunge"] ~~~ C2["2 machine compound<br/>leg press · chest press"] ~~~ C1["1 isolation<br/>curl · face pull · dead bug"]
  end
  subgraph EX["Same person, same rung positions, same four slots"]
    direction LR
    X1["Easy<br/>goblet squat · incline push-up<br/>band row · dead bug"] ~~~ X2["Normal<br/>back squat · floor push-up<br/>dumbbell row · plank"] ~~~ X3["Hard<br/>back squat · pike push-up<br/>weighted pull-up · hanging knee raise"]
  end
  Q --> TIME
